Z||000000||MISTER_PORKY||09-12-2001||09:26 PM||||HELLO FELLOW FIERO OWNERS. A BAD TIME, I KNOW, TO BE CAR SHOPING. MY THOUGHTS AND PARYERS ARE WITH ALL INVOLVED IN THE ATTACKS. FIRST OF ALL, I HAVE AN '84 FIERO THAT I BOUGHT NEW ALMOST 18 YEARS AGO. BEEN A GREAT CAR. I'M LNOW OOKING AT A FEW '88 GT's ALL WITH BETWEEN 30K & 40K MILES. I DO ALL MY OWN MECHANIC WORK. NOT AN EXPERT, DON'T KNOW MUCH ABOUT FIEROS. LIKE I SAID, MINE HAS BEEN A GREAT LITTLE CAR. HAVEN'T HAD TO DO MUCH TO IT IN THE PAST 113,000 MILES. TELL ME ANY SPECIFICS OR PROBLEM AREAS WITH '88's THAT I NEED TO BE AWARE OF AND LOOK FOR. ARE THE AUTOMATIC TRANNIES ANY GOOD. SEEMS LIKE MOST OF THE 88's I FIND HAVE THEM. MY CAR IS IN ALOMST MINT CONDIION SO I CAN'T USE IT AS A REFERENCE AS FAR AS PROBLEMS. WHAT'S THE BIGDIFFERENCES BETWEEN '87 & '88 OTHER THAN SUSPENSION & BRAKES ? WHAT WOULD IT COST TO BRING AN '87 UP TO PAR. I MAY CONSIDER BUYING AN '87. ALSO ARE ALL '87 & '88 5 SPEEDS GETRAG EQUIPPED ? PLAESE BE SERIOUS AND ALL INFO WILL BE GREATLY APPRECIATED. THANKS !!!!!!  ||||reg||10
Z||000001||Raydar||09-12-2001||10:50 PM||||Where to begin...<P>The big difference between the 87 and 88 is of course the suspension. <BR>The V-6 also gets internal balancing in 88, which means the flywheel is zero (or neutral) balanced. If you swap to a 3.4, you're gonna need that flywheel.<BR>Al 87 & 88 manual tranny GTs came with the Getrag. <BR>The 87 - 88 cars also got the redesigned headlight motors. Can rebuild 'em in about 1/2 hour. All solid state electronics instead of the conglomeration of relays.<BR>Automatic trannys are okay. I've had three 88 automatics. The only real problem I've noticed are the d@mn TCC solenoids like to stick, sometimes. Just like stopping while forgetting to push in the clutch. <BR>Had that happen on two of my three. <BR>There may be a few folks on here that have broken their auto tranny, but not near the number who have had problems with their clutch and its hydraulics.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"><P>Oh. YOU DON'T HAVE TO YELL!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Welcome to the forum.<P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"<BR></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000002||SLYGUY||09-13-2001||03:51 AM||||First and foremost....Welcome to the board.<BR>Secondly, I had an red '86 SEV6 with a 4 spd. Great car. <P>As you can see by the pic, I found this '88 GT with a 5 spd. Fantastic car. <BR>It has 100K miles, but the car is nearly perfect all the way 'round. I had to rebuild the driver's side headlight actuator, and it was easy. Only about 1/2 an hours work. <BR>Changed the alternator....again easy.<BR>I'm still working on getting the cruise up and running, and I have to replace the driver's quarter window. <BR>Besides the above, I am so happy I searched long and far for the 88. I had to drive 85 miles to get this one, but it was in the best condition. I would stick with the Getrag 5 speed myself. Why do they put autos in sports cars anyhow? I prefer to row my own anyways. For $4500 bucks, how can you ***** ?<P>Again, welcome<P>Sly<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/SLYGUYSIG.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Steve Normington||09-13-2001||11:01 AM||||FYI, it is going to be harder to find suspension and brake parts for the 88's because they don't share with any other vehicles.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Alex4mula||09-13-2001||01:25 PM||||Maybe hard to find "cheap" but NOT hard to find. I have never had any problem finding suspension/brake parts for my 88. Don't let that stop you for getting one. Stockwise they are the best.<p>[This message has been edited by Alex4mula (edited 09-13-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||Formula||09-13-2001||02:32 PM||||not to hard to find parts for, not as easy as the pre 88s but not any harder then your everyday 1994 Lamborghini Diablo SV 1 of 3 made car.....ok, maybe easier then a part for that but really its not that hard.<P>I put all new suspension and braking parts on mine, with a new motor, new cradle, new, paint, etc... and nothing was too hard to find.  if all else fails just check with the fiero store.<P>------------------<BR>         <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Formulasigfile.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||MISTER_PORKY||09-13-2001||08:44 PM||||THANKS FOR THE RESPONSE FOLKS !<BR>     FIRST OF ALL, FORGIVE ME FOR TYPING IN ALL CAPS. I'VE BEEN DOING IT FOR 20 YEARS. NOT "YELLING" AT ANYONE, SO DON'T TAKE IT PERSONALLY ! ANYWAY, I'M GOING ON A 300 MILE TRIP SATURDAY TO LOOK AT AN '88 GT T-TOP CAR WITH AUTOMATIC TRANSAXLE. I'VE HEARD GOOD AND BAD ABOUT THE GETRAG 5 SPEEDS. I THINK I'D STILL RATHER HAVE THE 5, BUT WHEN IT COMES TO A T-TOP, I DON'T THINK I CAN BE TO CHOOSEY. AND I REALLY DON'T MIND THE AUTOMATIC. EVERYTHING YOU ALL HAVE TOLD ME, I PRETTY MUCH ALREADY KNEW. REMEMBER, I HAVE AN '84 THAT I BOUGHT BRAND NEW ON FRIDAY 13th OF APRIL 1984. AND GUESS WHAT COLOR IT IS ! BLACK !!!!!!! HAS BEEN A GREAT CAR. WHO SAYS BLACK AND FRIDAY 13th ARE UNLUCKY ? <BR>    BUT AGAIN, IF ANYONE KNOWS OF ANY QUIRKS, BAD THINGS THAT ARE UNIQUE TO FIEROS OR '88 GT'S OR T-TOP CARS IN PARTICULAR, PLEASE LET ME KNOW BY TOMORROW NIGHT. IF I LIKE THIS CAR I'M GOING TO LOOK AT ON SATURDAY, I'M GOING TO BUY IT THEN. I'VE ALREADY LET 2 OF THEM GET AWAY FOR NOT BEING PERSISTANT.  <BR>   ALSO WHAT DO YOU THINK ABOUT THESE CARS AS FAR AS INVESTMENT ? IT SEEMS TO ME A LOT OF PEOPLE SEEM TO THINK THE '88 MODELS HAVE PRETTY MUCH BOTTOMED OUT IN ASKING PRICE AND ARE HEADED BACK UP. ESPECIALLY T-TOP MODELS. DON'T GET THE WRONG IDEA. I'M NOT HUNG UP ON T-TOP'S BUT IT WOULD BE NICE ! I'VE HAD CONVERTIBLES IN THE PAST ! AND I LIVE CLOSE TO THE BLUE RIDGE MOUNTAINS. HECK, I'M BUYING ONE TO DRIVE AND ENJOY. NOT TO SIT ON A PEDISTAL AND LOOK AT !<BR>    THANKS TO ALL, AND I THINK I'M REALLY GOING TO LIKE THIS PLACE ! I'VE ALREADY LEARNED QUITE A BIT JUST FROM READING WHAT YOU ALL HAVE ALREDY POSTED !<P>      .........PORKY.........<P>PS<BR>I'M PROUD TO BE AN AMERICAN ! GOD BLESS THE U.S.A. ! MY THOUGHTS AND PRAYERS ARE WITH ALL THOSE INVOLVED IN THE NEW YORK ATTACK !||||reg||1
